---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure | Access Free Tools"
  description="Learn how Access Free Tools handles advertising, affiliate links, product callouts, and sponsored relationships."
  path="/advertising-disclosure/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Advertising Disclosure</p>
    <h1>Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p>Tools stay free. Clearly disclosed advertising can help cover hosting and testing.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow legal-copy">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 20, 2026</p>

    <h2>HilltopAds advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools shows ads from HilltopAds after you choose to allow ads. That means one
      labeled banner near the end of a page and a small notification-style ad that you can close.
      We do not use pop-unders or full-page ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      HilltopAds chooses the advertiser. An ad is not a recommendation or an endorsement of the
      product or claim shown. Ads stay off private admin pages and APIs, and they never change a
      tool's formulas or results.
    </p>

    <h2>Infolinks contextual advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Infolinks advertising is not active. Our publisher application was not approved, so the
      integration is disabled. InText is a format that marks selected words with a double underline
      and can show a sponsored advertisement when a reader interacts with them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Infolinks chooses the advertised words and advertiser. Access Free Tools does not write those
      links as recommendations, and an ad is not an endorsement of the product or claim shown.
    </p>

    <h2>Where Infolinks is kept out</h2>
    <p>
      Infolinks is blocked from private admin pages, APIs, tool input and result areas, the Ask
      conversation, contact forms, navigation, and the footer. This keeps advertising out of text a
      visitor types or generates and away from the controls needed to use a tool.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <p>
      HilltopAds scripts load only after you press Allow ads. Choosing Keep ads off, or sending a
      Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, keeps them off. You can change your choice from
      the footer. No Infolinks or AdSense advertising scripts load while those accounts are
      unapproved. The <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>
      explains saved preferences and other privacy choices.
    </p>

    <h2>Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      AdSense advertising is not active. The site contains a disabled manual-placement path for a
      small calculator-page pilot, but it will not load without a real publisher ID, slot ID,
      approved account state, and required Google-certified consent setup. Infolinks and AdSense
      will not run on the same page during that pilot.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      No affiliate campaign is active. In future, I may add a clearly identified affiliate link and
      earn a commission when someone chooses to buy through it, at no extra cost to that person.
      Affiliate disclosures should appear close to affiliate links so the relationship is clear
      before anyone decides to open one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ads, affiliate links, and product previews do not change calculator formulas or results.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For advertising or affiliate disclosure questions, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      page or email <a href="mailto:contact@accessfreetools.com">contact@accessfreetools.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
